MRI is the most robust and powerful cancer-detection tool in the world, yet systems cost millions to purchase, take months to install, and require high levels of technical skill to operate. We've redesigned MRI from the ground up with new physics, algorithms, and hardware, all to bring cancer screening to the entire world. 

Our mobile MRI is an imaging clinic on wheels. No equipment to buy, no infrastructure needed. For a flat per-scan fee, any medical site can offer MRI cancer screening. Starting with prostate cancer. Then everything else.", 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'one_liner': {'value': 'Cancer screening without barriers', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'tags': [{'value': 'Hardware', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Medical Devices', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Health & Wellness', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}]}

{'name': {'value': 'Salesgraph', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'website': {'value': 'https://www.salesgraph.com/', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'all_locations': {'value': 'San Francisco, CA, USA', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'long_description': {'value': "Salesgraph equips reps with the most relevant context throughout the deal stage, providing proactive pre-call notes and post-call next steps. Sellers are CEOs of their deals; they need to know who the buyer is, what triggered them to take the first call, what their pain points are, how much value this new tool is bringing, are there any technical blockers, etc. 

A sale is only good when it doesn't feel like a sale to your customer, but rather the sales rep solved a problem for the customer. This was the problem Ricardo and I solved at Mintlify. We created a business case generator that took in call recordings, background news triggers and job updates, Mintlify's ROI and Pricing calculator, past deals won, and customer case studies --> produced a 3 page document expressing the value Mintlify provided + why the quote presented is justifiable. In doing so we closed more enterprise deals at a higher ACV as our champion was able to build a better purchasing case internally. 

Our goal is to empower every sales team to close deals at a higher ACV, while making sure reps learn from their mistakes and create a smooth sales experience for their end customer. ", 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'one_liner': {'value': 'the context layer for fast moving sales teams', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'tags': [{'value': 'SaaS', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'B2B', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Sales', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}]}

{'name': {'value': 'Saffron', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'former_names': [{'value': 'Saffron AI', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}], 'website': {'value': 'https://www.trysaffron.ai/', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'all_locations': {'value': 'San Francisco, CA, USA', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'long_description': {'value': "Saffron allows companies to quickly evaluate how well software engineers use AI to code. 

The way engineers write code has fundamentally changed, but the way companies evaluate them hasn't. Saffron gives teams full visibility into how candidates use AI agents to build, debug, and ship real features on an actual codebase. 

Saffron was founded by Robert Chondro (formerly MIT and Jane Street), Jerry Yao (Stanford and Jane Street), and Kazuma Choji (Harvey Mudd, published in NeurIPS and ICML), and is backed by Y Combinator (P26) and Afore Capital. ", 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'one_liner': {'value': 'Helping your company find 10x engineers. ', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'tags': [{'value': 'SaaS', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Human Resources', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'HR Tech', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}]}

{'name': {'value': 'matforge', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'former_names': [{'value': 'MatForge', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Matforge', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}], 'website': {'value': 'https://matforge.ai/', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'all_locations': {'value': 'San Francisco, CA, USA', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'long_description': {'value': 'We build AI scientists that discover new materials for the semiconductor industry - specifically datacenters and fabs. Finding novel materials today takes 10+ years of lab work. We aim to compress that timeline to months, using a swarm of AI agents.

Akash completed his PhD at Stanford on material discovery for semiconductors. The materials he discovered for nanoscale interconnects have been adopted into the roadmaps of Intel and TSMC. Advaith was the founding applied scientist at Persona AI (acquired by Luma Labs), where he built long horizon autonomous agents for major telecom and crypto companies.

Power consumption and heat release from AI chips is doubling every year. The semiconductor industry needs new materials to keep this exponential going - Matforge will help find them. ', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'one_liner': {'value': 'AI scientists to discover semiconductor materials', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'tags': [{'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Advanced Materials', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Semiconductors', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'AI', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}]}

{'name': {'value': 'Dispatch', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'website': {'value': 'https://dispatch.space/', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'all_locations': {'value': '', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'long_description': {'value': 'Dispatch is building refurbishable reentry vehicles that host and return payloads for companies making ultra-high-value materials (semiconductors, biotech, and pharma) that can only be manufactured in space. Right now, these companies have no practical way to manufacture and get their products back to Earth. We solve this bottleneck.

We just returned from the Mojave Desert testing our first full-scale reentry heat shield designed to protect the satellite as it returns from space at Mach 20+, built in an apartment for 100x cheaper than competitors. To test, we held it behind a rocket engine to simulate the forces of atmospheric reentry. IT WORKED! Watch here - https://youtu.be/dhlQmnIoptg

To scale, we anchor permanent infrastructure in orbit - building high power Autonomous Space Stations designed from day one for "lights-out" manufacturing serviced by the reentry vehicles.', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'one_liner': {'value': 'Satellites for manufacturing in space', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, 'tags': [{'value': 'Manufacturing', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Aerospace', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}, {'value': 'Advanced Materials', 'matchLevel': 'none', 'matchedWords': []}]}

